GIVEN key IS A STRING
      entries IS A LIST OF Provision
GIVETH A MAYBE Provision
`the provision with key` key `among` entries MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN entry FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF entry's `provision key` EQUALS key
        THEN JUST entry
        ELSE `the provision with key` key `among` rest

GIVEN key IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE Provision
`the provision indexed as` key MEANS
    `the provision with key` key `among` `the provision index`

GIVEN key IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the heading as printed of provision` key MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision indexed as` key
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN JUST (entry's `heading as printed`)

GIVEN key IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is indexed` key MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision indexed as` key
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST entry THEN TRUE

-- Tests. Expected values are counts and headings read from the text by hand and by the script that wrote the entries.
#ASSERT count `the provision index` EQUALS 621
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a section`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a subsection`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 155
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a paragraph`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 204
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a subparagraph`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 45
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a Schedule`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a Schedule clause`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 16
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `kind of provision` EQUALS `a defined term`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 120
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `shown only as dots`) `the provision index`) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the heading as printed of provision` "1" EQUALS JUST "Short title"
